<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<Defs>

  <!--
    INHABITED_TILEMUTATOR_NO_ENTRY_1: the wilderness Inhabited_Place route's only
    way in. WorldObjects_Inhabited.xml says it plainly: "This def places the
    company; the mutator places the set", but until this def existed, no
    TileMutatorDef anywhere named Inhabited_Cast or RM_InhabitedStock, so
    MapGeneratorDefOf.Encounter ran with neither GenStep in its list. A place
    could hold a full roster and a full larder and still generate an empty map.

    ⚠️ Per GenSteps_Inhabited.xml's own warning: naming Inhabited_Cast without
    RM_InhabitedStock generates people with no goods, silently. Both are here.

    No chanceOnNonLandmarkTile: this campaign has no worldgen
    (design/Jawa/worldbuilding/the_one_map.md) so nothing should roll this by
    chance. It is assigned to a specific Ash'karr tile by hand, through the
    bridge's world-editing tools, the same way RSW_MoistureFarm is.
  -->
  <TileMutatorDef>
    <defName>RM_InhabitedPlace</defName>
    <label>inhabited place</label>
    <description>Someone has made a home of this ground.</description>
    <extraGenSteps>
      <li>Inhabited_Cast</li>
      <li>RM_InhabitedStock</li>
    </extraGenSteps>
  </TileMutatorDef>

</Defs>
